From b67b05adbd615beb810546b3367b7d759d2915da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:42:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 67/98] pco: fold constant trailing channels of 8-bit UNORM
 pixel outputs

The pck that packs a pixel output issues once per packed channel, and
the constants it packs need a mov into consecutive temps first. For
four 8-bit linear UNORM channels, pack only the leading non-constant
channels and insert them into the packed bits of the constant trailing
ones (alpha = 1.0 is the common case); an output with only constant
channels becomes an immediate. A pck of fewer than four channels leaves
the other bytes undefined, hence the insert (one msk + logical group)
rather than an OR, and the leading channels are rebuilt from their own
sources (pco mistranslated a vec3 of another vec4's channels). Runs late in pco_postprocess_nir; a bcsel between two equal
constants (what alpha-to-one leaves for alpha = 1.0) counts as constant.

vkrender gradient shader, vec4(fract(x/64), fract(y/64), 0.25, 1.0) to
RGBA8: mov + pck x4 (5 issues) -> pck x2 + insert (3 issues), 7 -> 5 issues
in all. BXM-4-64, 2048x2048 render pass: 2.20 -> 1.75 ms batched, 2.31
-> 1.98 ms with a fence wait per frame. Fragment shading here is bound
by ALU issue rate (~0.24 ms per issue per 2048x2048 pass).
A constant-colour shader goes from 9 issues (alpha-to-one select + mov +
pck x4) to a single immediate write: 2.68 -> 1.48 ms batched.

NaN constants are left to the hardware conversion; sRGB and SNORM
formats are not folded. vkrender pixel-exact check passes at 512/2048.
CTS (5062 + 9170 + 838 + 282 cases): identical to before; gate 44/44.
